{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:5Tries4TrieV","title":"Trie","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tries\/Trie.swift#L26","fileName":"Trie.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are sequences of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, stored as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" holds words,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" the same words scalar by scalar, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" byte strings. Lookup,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for a key of "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and at most "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"type":"text","text":" children per vertex. A trie answers the queries a hash set cannot: every key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a prefix, whether any key has one, and the longest key that is a prefix of a query."}]},{"code":["let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the trie holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960)."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/d